Update procedure:
  npm pack pdfjs-dist@<version>
  tar -xzf pdfjs-dist-<version>.tgz package/legacy/build/pdf.mjs package/legacy/build/pdf.worker.mjs package/LICENSE
  # copy pdf.mjs -> vendor/pdfjs/pdf.js, pdf.worker.mjs -> vendor/pdfjs/pdf.worker.js, LICENSE -> vendor/pdfjs/LICENSE
  # Renamed to .js on purpose: many servers send .mjs with a MIME type browsers refuse for module scripts.
  # assets/js/verification.js imports ../../vendor/pdfjs/pdf.js and Utils/Assets.php points the worker at
  # vendor/pdfjs/pdf.worker.js, so copying under the .mjs names would leave the OLD pdf.js in use, silently.
  # update this VERSION file: version, dates, "Tarball integrity" (npm pack --json prints it) and the SHA-256
  # list (Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 vendor/pdfjs/*) — build.ps1 fails until the list matches the new files
Then re-check that assets/js/verification.js's API usage (getDocument/getPage/getTextContent/
GlobalWorkerOptions) is still compatible — see CHANGELOG entries between the old and new version for
any [api-major]/[api-minor] breaking changes.
